# Fathom

## Overview

Fathom is a bioluminescent deep-sea maze chase for the browser. The player is a
small glowing forager threading the flooded corridors of a pitch-dark maze,
grazing plankton while predators hunt it. The maze is unseen until the forager's
own light or a sonar pulse touches it, so a dive is as much about sensing where
the danger is as about outswimming it.

Fathom's defining idea is hunting in the dark. The maze starts unrevealed and is
uncovered as the forager explores it or pings it, the predators stay hidden
between glimpses, and each predator hunts by a different sense. One tracks
light, one tracks sound, and one hunts in the flash of its own flare.

Fathom has its own name, look, sensing systems, and predators, and its assets,
branding, and design are original to it.

